 plans for 2027 are up (Pellham +18%, Norvane +12%). Data-centre grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026 (n2).\n- **Financing is the main risk, and it's concentrated in Pellham.**\n  - Utilities make up 62% of VLTX orders. Pellham is 35% of that and Norvane is 21%.\n  - Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B share offering. It now says it will cut transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes \"until financing improves.\"\n  - The 18% capex plan therefore looks unreliable. That plan is what the demand case for VLTX rests on.\n  - Norvane looks fine. It priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably.\n  - Debt is open but costs more, with spreads 30bp wider in Q3. Equity is mostly closed (n3).\n\n**What would change this:**\n- Pellham relaunches its equity raise on better terms, or finances through debt, and restores the deferred orders.\n- Implied volatility falls back below its median.\n\n**Limits of the evidence:**\n- I had no strike-level premiums, liquidity or term-structure data, and no comparison of implied with realized volatility.\n- I had no order backlog or equipment pricing data.\n- I found no bond, leverage or rating data for Pellham, so I can't say whether debt could replace its withdrawn equity raise.\n- Everything rests on a few short documents.\n\nSources: n2.r1, n3.r1, n4.r1.","ttft_ms":2767,"type":"result","duration_ms":44727,"uuid":"011cca4f-d909-4e40-b1eb-4e7b38f96cc9","ttft_stream_ms":1584,"time_to_request_ms":515,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":15,"system_prompt":12,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":37,"input_attachments":133,"input_hooks":26,"conversation_append":6,"transcript_persist":62,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":62,"init_frame_send":10,"engine_pickup":11,"loop_entry":17,"message_prep":9,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":42,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":8,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":9,"client_creation":19,"request_build":20},"turn_start_resum